  'hla antigen' => 'A cell-surface human leukocyte antigen encoded by the major histocompatibility complex that presents peptides to T cells and influences transplant compatibility and immune disease risk.',
  'holter electrocardiography' => 'Continuous ambulatory ECG recording, usually for 24 hours or longer, used to detect intermittent arrhythmias, correlate symptoms with rhythm, and assess heart-rate patterns.',
  'homeopathy' => 'An alternative-health system that uses highly diluted preparations selected according to “like cures like”; reliable evidence has not shown homeopathic products to treat serious disease beyond placebo effects.',
  'homozygote' => 'An individual or cell carrying two identical alleles at a particular gene locus, whether the alleles are normal, pathogenic, or another variant.',
  'hordeolum' => 'A tender, localized infection or inflammation of an eyelid gland, commonly called a stye, producing a painful red lump near the eyelid margin.',
  'hounsfield unit' => 'A CT attenuation value that expresses tissue density relative to water, conventionally assigning air about -1000 HU, water 0 HU, and dense bone positive values.',
  'hyperbilirubinemia' => 'An abnormally high concentration of bilirubin in blood that may cause jaundice; causes include hemolysis, impaired liver processing, hepatocellular injury, and bile-duct obstruction.',
  'hypercalciuria' => 'Excessive urinary calcium excretion, which can promote calcium kidney stones and, in some settings, bone mineral loss; evaluation considers diet, medications, kidney function, and endocrine causes.',
  'hyperglycinemia' => 'An abnormally high glycine concentration in blood, most notably in nonketotic hyperglycinemia, a disorder of glycine cleavage that can cause neonatal hypotonia, seizures, and developmental impairment.',
  'hyperhomocysteinemia' => 'An elevated blood homocysteine concentration associated with genetic enzyme defects, folate or vitamin B12 deficiency, kidney disease, medicines, and increased vascular or pregnancy-related risk in selected settings.',
  'hyperkeratosis' => 'Thickening of the outer keratin layer of skin or mucosa, producing callus, scale, or rough plaques in response to friction, inflammation, infection, inherited disorders, or other causes.',
  'hyperlordosis' => 'Exaggerated inward curvature of the lumbar spine, often producing a swayback appearance and sometimes associated with pain, muscular imbalance, obesity, pregnancy, or structural spinal disease.',
  'hypernatremia result' => 'A high blood sodium result, usually reflecting too little free water relative to body sodium; severity and rate of onset determine neurologic risk and the urgency and speed of correction.',
  'hyperoxaluria' => 'Excess oxalate production or absorption leading to high urinary oxalate, calcium oxalate stones, nephrocalcinosis, and in severe inherited forms progressive kidney injury.',
  'hyperoxia' => 'Exposure to an abnormally high oxygen concentration or tissue oxygen level, which can cause oxygen toxicity, absorption atelectasis, retinal injury in premature infants, or lung injury depending on dose and duration.',
